# Still excluded, each for a specific reason rather than a blanket "not updated for Rigor":
#   coinselector_tests  - check_max_weight builds a tx that exceeds MAX_STANDARD_TX_WEIGHT because
#                         Rigor inputs (Ed25519, 32-byte keys) are heavier than the ECDSA sizes the
#                         fixture was tuned for.
#   feebumper_tests     - external_max_weight_test fixtures are P2PKH/P2SH-P2WPKH/P2WPKH/P2WSH with
#                         ECDSA signatures, which the Rigor interpreter rejects outright.
#   ismine_tests        - exercises LegacyScriptPubKeyMan and Bitcoin script/descriptor forms; also
#                         dereferences a null descriptor when parsing fails.
#   psbt_wallet_tests   - SIGABRT in psbt_updater_test and parse_hd_keypath (not yet diagnosed).
#   spend_tests         - SubtractFee hardcodes Bitcoin fee/vsize expectations, and
#                         wallet_duplicated_preset_inputs_test no longer rejects duplicate inputs.
#   wallet_tests        - ListCoinsTest aborts on the m_buffering assertion in Logger::StartLogging
#                         and the suite then hangs.
BITCOIN_TEST_SUITE += \
  wallet/test/init_test_fixture.cpp \
  wallet/test/init_test_fixture.h \
  wallet/test/wallet_test_fixture.cpp \
  wallet/test/wallet_test_fixture.h

